# RTK (Rust Token Killer) Automation Rule for Cline & Roo Code

Whenever executing terminal commands:
- Always prefix commands with `rtk` (e.g., `rtk git status`, `rtk npm test`, `rtk cargo test`, `rtk pytest`, `rtk vitest`, `rtk ls`, `rtk rg`).
- RTK condenses bulky compiler/build/test outputs to conserve precious context tokens without losing error details or exit status.
- Keep the prefix in chained commands: `rtk git add . && rtk git commit -m "msg"`.
- Use `rtk gain` to inspect token savings metrics.
